      "id": "thm-coordinate-ring-principal-open",
      "location": "Proof step 1.3",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "The step states: “Because $D_X(\\overline h_i)\\subseteq D_X(\\overline f)$, every point of $X$ at which $h_i$ vanishes also makes $f$ vanish. Equivalently, $V(I(X)+(h_i))\\subseteq V(I(X)+(f))$.” The implication has the containment direction reversed. For $X=\\mathbf A_k^1$, $\\overline f=\\overline t$, and $\\overline h=\\overline{t(t-1)}$, one has $D_X(\\overline h)\\subseteq D_X(\\overline f)$, but at $t=1$, $h=0$ and $f=1$, so $V((h))\\nsubseteq V((f))$. Thus the cited Nullstellensatz cannot yield $f\\in\\sqrt{I(X)+(h_i)}$ or $\\overline f^{N_i}=\\overline c_i\\overline h_i$. The invalid relation is then used to form the common-denominator expressions $a_i/\\overline f^N$ required for the surjectivity proof.",
      "severity": "fatal",
